[00:16.36] The word you learn to love (The disapproval that you hate)
[00:19.00] That's Mother (From Mother)
[00:21.09] They teach you to respect... (Makes you always want to please)
[00:23.26] Mother (Mother)
[00:24.78] The one who keeps you warm (The one who keeps you warm)
[00:26.77] And shelters you from harm (And shelters you from harm)
[00:28.82] Watch out she'll stunt your mind (She'll open up your mind)
[00:30.82] 'Til you emulate her kind (To make you good and make you kind)
[00:33.17] Is that Mother? (Mother)
[00:48.56] Downstairs I don't know (Downstairs I don't know)
[00:51.04] If it's the springs in her bed (Why I feel safe in my bed)
[00:53.26] Or her joints I hear (When I know I'm alone)
[00:55.61] Creaking overhead (She must be watching overhead)
[00:57.36] Mother (Mother)
[01:14.58] She'll twist the words you speak (She'll kiss and say goodbye)
[01:16.96] If she thinks you're near escape (If you want to go away)
[01:18.75] Mother (Mother)
[01:23.23] So she clutches at her brood (So she gathers up her brood)
[01:25.54] And sits across its face (And smiles into their face)
[01:27.90] She sucks up all its energy (She beams down vital energy)
[01:30.38] And smothers their last breath (She gave us our first breath)
[01:32.44] Oh Mother (Mother)
[01:37.89] The thing you grow to hate (The love you won't forget)
